        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lemma</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In lean.nvim the document_symbol binding (default <code>gO</code>) yields only <code>a</code> and <code>c</code>:</p>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/CnTsyXOluSE8PgxtcXdaoXjP/Screenshot_20260508-112754.png\">Screenshot_20260508-112754.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/CnTsyXOluSE8PgxtcXdaoXjP/Screenshot_20260508-112754.png\" title=\"Screenshot_20260508-112754.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"2400x465\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/CnTsyXOluSE8PgxtcXdaoXjP/Screenshot_20260508-112754.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p>This is a little unfair as <code>lemma</code> is in Mathlib not core, so it doesn't make sense as a builtin.<br>\nStill, Mathlib has a 2:5 lemma:theorem ratio (which iiuc is mostly older code), and this makes document symbol lookup feel \"unpredictably flaky\".</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Feature request: a way to instruct the LSP server (e.g. via lakefile or CLI arguments) to treat certain <code>command</code>s/macros as \"declaration-like\". </p>\n<p>Perhaps this would also be useful for non-attr code generation macros.</p>\n<p>(EDIT: I have assumed that this is the LSP server not lean.nvim, given that lemma is custom syntax to begin with.)</p>",
        "id": 593664889,
